    {
      "id": "msg_011CfNrwo4qm9Y1xLCcyGNsL-1",
      "kind": "message",
      "role": "agent",
      "text": "This is \"calc\", a tiny JavaScript calculator library that exports `add` and `mul` from `src/math.js`, with `test.js` checking them using `node:assert/strict`. The README says it's used by the Skaro agent probe.\n\n`add` is broken: it returns `a - b` (`src/math.js:2`), so `assert.equal(add(2, 3), 5)` in `test.js:5` should fail, because `add(2, 3)` gives -1. I didn't change anything.\n\nThe claude.ai Google Drive connector needs to be authorized in your claude.ai connector settings before it can be used.",
      "phase": "final",
      "status": "done",
      "native": {
